            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="certifried-studio">8. CertiFried Studio</h2>
                <p>CertiFried Studio is the Windows app for the stream bot. These terms apply to the official builds we publish on the <a href="/downloads/studio">download page</a>:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Unsigned builds.</strong> Studio is not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen warns about it the first time it runs. We publish the SHA-256 checksum of every build next to it and in <code>SHA256SUMS.txt</code>. Download Studio only from certifriedmultitool.com and compare the checksum before running it if you are unsure. A file whose checksum does not match is not ours.</li>
                    <li><strong>Updates.</strong> The installed app checks our site for updates, downloads them, and checks each one against the SHA-512 hash in our update feed before installing it. You can turn update checks off in Studio&rsquo;s Settings. The portable app does not update itself.</li>
                    <li><strong>Your PC and your OBS.</strong> Studio acts on your PC and in OBS on your instructions: it switches scenes, plays sounds, presses keys and listens for voice commands when you turn them on. To keep song requests out of your VODs it adds a music source and sets OBS&rsquo;s VOD track while you are offline, after backing up the profile file; everything else it changes in OBS only when you click. <a href="/studio/how-it-works#changes-to-obs">How it works</a> lists these changes. Keep your own backups of anything you cannot afford to lose.</li>
                    <li><strong>Data.</strong> What Studio stores on your PC and sends to us is described exactly on <a href="/studio/privacy">Studio privacy</a>. Studio contains no analytics, telemetry or advertising.</li>
                    <li><strong>Builds from elsewhere.</strong> You may build Studio yourself from the source, or use someone else&rsquo;s build, under the AGPL. We can only vouch for the builds we publish, and our support covers those.</li>
                    <li><strong>Uninstalling.</strong> Uninstalling leaves Studio&rsquo;s settings folder so a reinstall keeps them; delete <code>%APPDATA%\CertiFried Studio</code> to remove them, and revoke the device on the dashboard&rsquo;s Devices page.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

